VERDICT: state-canon is WELL-DEFINED but NARROW in scope

Definition Quality:
  Clarity:      ████████████████████ 100% — Crystal clear
  Completeness: ████████████████████ 100% — Complete for its scope
  Testability:  ████████████████████ 100% — Tests exist and pass
  Documentation: ████████████████████ 100% — Excellent (README, INTERFACE, METHODOLOGY)

Scope Assessment:
  As a "canon layer":    ████████████████████ 100% — Does exactly what it claims
  As a VSM component:    ████████████░░░░░░░░ 60% — Missing VSM-aware features
  As part of VSF system: ████████░░░░░░░░░░░░ 40% — Missing many integrations
  As standalone package: ████████████████████ 100% — Perfect for public release

RECOMMENDATION:
  state-canon is EXCELLENT as an agnostic, public package. It should NOT be
  modified to include VSF-specific features — those belong in a VSM-specific
  wrapper. The current definition is correct and complete for its purpose.

  The gaps identified above are INTEGRATION GAPS, not definition gaps.
  They belong in a vsf-state-canon-extension package, not in state-canon itself.


═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
                       SECTION 7: PACKAGE STRATEGY
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

STRATEGY: Two-Layer Architecture

Layer 1: state-canon-mcp (PUBLIC, AGNOSTIC)
  ──────────────────────────────────────────
  What: Core canon layer for any agent
  Where: github.com/rm-w3kufe/state-canon-mcp
  Status: READY FOR PUBLIC RELEASE
  Features: StateProvider, Reconciler, Digest, MCP Server
  Dependencies: None (stdlib only)
  Tests: 6 passing (E2E, Freshness, Focus, Housekeeping)

Layer 2: vsf-state-canon (PRIVATE, VSM-SPECIFIC)
  ───────────────────────────────────────────────
  What: VSM-aware extensions for state-canon
  Where: ~/vsf/scripts/shared/ (existing code)
  Status: NEEDS PACKAGING
  Features:
    - Tree execution (from socratic-engine)
    - VSM block parsing (from vslline.py)
    - Policy enforcement (from vsf_policy_enforcement.py)
    - NATS integration (from vsf_nats_pipeline.py)
    - Cybernetic cycle (from vsf_cybernetic_cycle.py)
  Dependencies: state-canon-mcp, socratic-engine, nats-py
  Tests: 281 passing (existing)

Integration Point:
  The bridge (StateCanonBridge) already connects the two layers.
  The VSM-specific wrapper imports state-canon and extends it.


